  "_what": "The FMU's variable table, as data. A value reference is the only thing that ties a modelDescription entry to a line of C, and a mismatch is silent in both directions: the master sets 'angle' and the wrapper reads a duty. So the table lives here once, and two independent readers are checked against it -- the XML a master parses, and the enum the wrapper switches on.",
  "_who_reads_it": "api/fmu/modelDescription.xml_check.py, run by `.github/project/gates.py fmu` before it builds anything. Adding a variable means adding it here first; the check then refuses an XML or a wrapper that disagrees.",
  "step_s": 5e-05,
  "step_source": "1 / pwm_freq_hz of the motor the wrapper creates: the fixed communication step is the loop's own period, read back from the motor rather than written twice (fmu_wrapper.c, exitInitializationMode).",
